# SRP, SOLID, and readable production code

## Single responsibility

- One file, one reason to change. Split factories, mappers, transport adapters, and types.
- Functions do one thing; name them after that thing (`mapPromptToOpenAiMessages`, not `prepare`).
- Prefer a thin orchestrator that calls focused helpers over a god class.

## SOLID (practical)

- **S** — Keep modules small; extract when a unit mixes mapping, I/O, and policy.
- **O** — Add behavior via new helpers/adapters; avoid growing `if` trees in the entrypoint.
- **L** — Implement published contracts (e.g. AI SDK `LanguageModel`) without surprising callers.
- **I** — Depend on narrow ports (`complete(...)`), not fat Nest services, when only one method is needed.
- **D** — Callers inject the port; helpers stay free of Nest DI unless DI is the product.

## Production grade

- Validate config at the boundary; fail fast with clear errors.
- Preserve abort/`AbortSignal` end to end; merge caller + call-site signals when both exist.
- Map unsupported features to SDK warnings or `UnsupportedFunctionalityError` — never silent drop of required behavior.
- Unit-test helpers in isolation with mocked ports; mirror paths under `tests/`.
- Public barrels export only the intended API; keep internals private to the folder.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — domain calls provider HTTP or hand-rolled doGenerate
await openAi.complete({ ... });
await fetch(`${baseUrl}/chat/completions`, { ... });

// ✅ GOOD — AI SDK model + generate helpers; infra only as fetch/scrub
createLanguageModel({ rateLimiter, config });
await generateText({ model, prompt }); // via helpers/generate when ready
```
